& [PresentBlockers] are non-substitutive
  + I03A Enterprise-signing release execution has not passed
  + jsonschema is absent from committed Cargo.lock
  + no I03 satisfaction record or active implementation phase lock exists
  + E3 trusted reviewer policy principals and catalogue are absent
  + exact E compile-time fixture inventory is absent
  + conversation mailbox access is unavailable and repository continuity cannot claim delivery

& [DependencyEdgeKinds] are closed
  + hard_prerequisite means consumer meaning or construction is invalid without completed predecessor output
  + governance_order means campaign serialization for auditability
  + integration_order means units must update the same ledger as exact successors
  + evidence_dependency means proof consumes exact predecessor evidence without gaining its runtime authority
  + each edge states one kind and cannot be upgraded implicitly

& [ActivationUnits] are exactly A B C D E1 E2 E3 and E
  + each binds one canonical specification and future active lock
  + each owns exclusive source tests interfaces limits and forbidden scope
  + each declares hard governance integration and evidence predecessors separately
  + each completes only through conjunctive implementation verification review satisfaction lock and evidence closure

& [ModuleOwnership] is singular
  + B owns crates/cantor_procedure_tool/src/json_ingress.rs
  + C owns crates/cantor_procedure_tool/src/residual_registry.rs
  + D owns crates/cantor_procedure_tool/src/reader_observation.rs and CantorDenyRetriever
  + E1 owns crates/cantor_procedure_tool/src/conformance/obligation.rs
  + E2 owns crates/cantor_procedure_tool/src/conformance/proposal.rs
  + E3 owns crates/cantor_procedure_tool/src/conformance/review.rs
  + E owns crates/cantor_procedure_tool/src/conformance/report.rs
  + no exclusive module has two semantic owners in one topology

& [TestOwnership] mirrors units
  + A owns crates/cantor_procedure_tool/tests/schema_validator_dependency.rs
  + B owns crates/cantor_procedure_tool/tests/json_ingress.rs
  + C owns crates/cantor_procedure_tool/tests/residual_registry.rs
  + D owns crates/cantor_procedure_tool/tests/reader_observation.rs
  + E1 owns crates/cantor_procedure_tool/tests/conformance_obligation.rs
  + E2 owns crates/cantor_procedure_tool/tests/conformance_proposal.rs
  + E3 owns crates/cantor_procedure_tool/tests/conformance_review.rs
  + E owns crates/cantor_procedure_tool/tests/conformance_report.rs

& [SharedIntegrationLedgers] are narrowly typed
  + workspace Cargo.toml Cargo.lock and procedure-tool Cargo.toml are A-only
  + crates/cantor_procedure_tool/src/lib.rs is a crate declaration cfg and re-export ledger
  + crates/cantor_procedure_tool/src/conformance/mod.rs is a conformance declaration and re-export ledger
  + constants algorithms validators record construction corpus policy and semantic behavior are forbidden in ledgers

& [IntegrationSteward] applies mechanical deltas only
  + validate future lease unit active lock predecessor identity and allowed anchors
  + validate complete reviewed InterfaceReceipt
  + apply only declared module feature gate and re-export statements
  + emit exact normalized delta and successor digest
  + refuse any semantic change ownership conflict stale base or scope expansion

& [SemanticOwner] authors one exclusive module
  + binds its specification interfaces imports exports faults resource limits and tests
  + emits an InterfaceReceipt candidate after its unit proof exists
  + cannot independently review or integrate its own work
  + cannot touch another unit module or shared ledger without separately authorized stewardship

& [TouchLeaseCandidate] is prospective and non-active
  + lease id unit id active lock exact predecessor allowed anchors delta limits semantic owner steward and status
  + status proposed issued consumed refused stale or superseded
  + issued requires future authority not present here
  + stale predecessor refuses and requires a successor source decision
  + this formation contains zero issued or consumed leases

& [InterfaceReceipt] is a future handoff boundary
  + exact unit module digest feature gate exports imports fault vocabulary resource profile forbidden dependencies test inventory and review identity
  + disposition complete challenged refused or superseded
  + a challenged refused incomplete or stale receipt cannot be integrated

& [UnitA] is dependency admission only
  + hard predecessor is exact completed I02C
  + future authority is exact signed active I03A Revision 1
  + exclusive mutations are workspace Cargo.toml Cargo.lock procedure-tool Cargo.toml and schema_validator_dependency.rs
  + it proves exact jsonschema family no resolver capabilities preflight deny behavior and host debug release gates
  + it creates no production ingress registry reader conformance corpus or report behavior

& [UnitB] is faithful byte ingress
  + governance predecessor is completed A and authority is separately active I03B
  + adds json_ingress.rs and focused test
  + leases lib.rs for one declaration and re-export delta
  + byte recognition performs no schema validation typed deserialization semantic execution or runtime I/O

& [UnitC] is semantic residual registry
  + governance predecessor is completed B and authority is separately active I03C
  + adds residual_registry.rs and focused test
  + leases lib.rs for one declaration and re-export delta
  + pure lookup never invokes a named function or creates enforcement authority

& [UnitD] is dual-reader observation
  + hard predecessors are completed A B and C and authority is separately active I03D
  + adds reader_observation.rs CantorDenyRetriever and focused test
  + leases lib.rs for one declaration and re-export delta
  + observations grant no compatibility or admission conclusion

& [UnitE1] is obligation compilation
  + hard predecessor is completed D and authority is separately active I03E1
  + creates conformance/mod.rs when absent and adds obligation.rs and focused test
  + leases lib.rs and conformance/mod.rs for declarations and re-exports
  + obligation output is neither proposal expectation review nor observation

& [UnitE2] is proposal generation
  + hard predecessor is completed E1 with exact obligation catalogue and authority is separately active I03E2
  + adds proposal.rs and focused test
  + leases conformance/mod.rs for one declaration and re-export delta
  + generated proposals are unsigned and cannot authorize expectations

& [UnitE3] is proof oracle and review
  + hard predecessor is completed E2 with exact proposal catalogue
  + authority also requires future trust policy authorized principals and separately active I03E3
  + adds review.rs and focused test
  + leases conformance/mod.rs for one declaration and re-export delta
  + review candidate formation grants no reader execution

& [UnitE] is replay and report assembly
  + hard predecessors are completed D E1 E2 and E3 and authority is separately active I03E
  + adds report.rs focused test and exact future compile-time corpus inventory
  + leases conformance/mod.rs for one declaration and re-export delta
  + permits only bounded effectless replay under its active authority and never automatic compatibility admission

& [DependencyDAG] is reconstructible
  * I02C hard-precedes A
  * A governance-precedes B
  * B governance-precedes C
  * A B and C hard-precede D
  * D hard-precedes E1
  * E1 hard-precedes E2
  * E2 hard-precedes E3
  * D E1 E2 and E3 hard-precede E
  + integration edges additionally serialize lib.rs and conformance/mod.rs successors
  + no cycle or documentary substitute is admitted

& [FixtureCustody] is content addressed
  + tests/fixtures/cpms_i03 is a candidate root only
  + future lock enumerates exact path role bytes digest generator lineage owner and review
  + source_seed mutation_proposal reviewed_expectation observation and comparison_golden roles remain distinct
  + shared use does not create shared ownership
  + no runtime discovery read write cache database or mutable update

& [WorkerPartition] is authority and path bounded
  + owner prepares only its unit exclusive files after activation
  + integration steward alone applies leased ledger changes
  + fixture steward admits only fully identified immutable fixtures
  + independent reviewer does not mutate reviewed implementation
  + parallel preparation is allowed only for disjoint files with satisfied prerequisites

& [GateVocabulary] is exact
  + observed_pass observed_fail observed_blocked not_run stale and not_applicable
  + compilation does not prove execution
  + blocked execution does not prove behavior failure
  + later success is a successor and never deletes preserved block evidence
  + host admission binds exact artifact environment policy command and observation

& [UnitCompletion] is conjunctive
  + canonical and active phase identity
  + exact source inventory and clean ownership
  + every requirement implemented and verified
  + independent completion review and project satisfaction record
  + active lock and evidence closure
  + required debug release formatting lint documentation advisory and host observations
  + any missing member leaves the unit incomplete

& [FailureAndRecovery] are non-destructive
  + failed blocked partial stale and superseded attempts remain durable
  + partial shared-ledger changes grant no downstream authority
  + recovery uses reviewed successor source and commit
  + destructive history rewrite is never prescribed

& [FiniteLimits] are mandatory before activation
  + at most 16 inputs 8 units 64 edges 64 surfaces 16 ledgers and 128 lease records
  + at most 256 imports and 256 exports per unit
  + at most 65536 fixture records and 4096 gate observations
  + path at most 1024 UTF-8 bytes and rationale at most 4096 UTF-8 bytes
  + checked arithmetic governs all counts totals joins and allocations

& [CanonicalIdentity] is deterministic
  + fixed field order lexical record order normalized repository-relative slash paths and domain-separated digests
  + normative identity excludes timestamps UI wording commentary hidden reasoning allocation address and working-tree enumeration order
  + indexes reconstruct from primary records and grant no authority

& [SuccessorRule] protects shape
  + path owner dependency kind feature interface fixture scope or authority change requires new preserved source SJS topology and review
  + exact predecessor records remain accessible
  + no edit mutates this topology in place after lock

& [FormationBoundary] is strict
  + source SJS canonical exploded requirements justification plan review inactive lock proof turn and evidence metadata only
  - never: TouchLease issuance InterfaceReceipt issuance Cargo mutation Rust implementation dependency activation untrusted parsing validation reader execution semantic invocation compatibility admission key generation signing provider model service persistence network notification effect production hardware FPGA or shared inference

& [Disposition] is canonical_formation_complete_implementation_refused
